1. MICROCONTROLLER
-------------------
Part: ESP32 (exact board variant TBD)
Role: Reads IR sensor array, runs line-following control loop,
      drives motor PWM via TB6612FNG.
Notes: 3.3V logic. Confirm ADC pin count vs sensor channels.
       No encoder feedback available (see Motors section) -
       control loop will run open-loop on motor speed.

2. IR SENSOR ARRAY
-------------------
Part: Analog straight IR sensor array (model/channel count TBD)
Role: Detects line position, feeds error value to control loop.
History: V1 used a curved array - dropped (hard to calibrate,
         hard to CAD). V2+ uses straight array - simpler math,
         simpler mounting.
Mounting: Fixed hole in V2 Final (no longer adjustable).
Open items: Channel count, sensor spacing, mount height - TBD.

3. MOTOR DRIVER
---------------
Part: TB6612FNG
Role: Drives both N20 motors independently (dual H-bridge).
Notes: Compatible with 3.3V logic from ESP32. Confirm motor
       supply voltage matches battery pack output.

4. MOTORS
---------
Part: N20 6V geared DC motors, NO encoder (x2)
Role: Drive wheels, differential steering.
Notes: Standard N20 motors without encoder feedback. Speed/
       position control will be open-loop (PWM duty cycle only,
       no closed-loop speed correction between left/right motor).
       Line-following error correction still comes from the IR
       array, but wheel speed mismatch (from motor tolerance,
       battery sag, friction) cannot be actively corrected
       without encoders.
Open items: Gear ratio, shaft diameter match with wheels, stall
            current. If closed-loop speed control is needed later,
            would require swapping to encoder-equipped N20 motors
            or adding an external speed-sensing method.

5. WHEELS
---------
Part: High-traction wheels, 32mm diameter (x2)
Role: Primary drive wheels on N20 motor shafts.
Open items: Confirm hub bore matches motor shaft (typically 3mm
            D-shaft). Confirm clearance with chassis/caster mount.

6. CASTER BALL MOUNT
---------------------
Part: Caster ball mount (Caster_Ball_Mount.SLDPRT)
Role: Third ground-contact point, rotates freely, keeps chassis
      level and stable during turns.
Status: Scratch/working file - used to test motor mount spacing
        and final caster height before locking into main chassis.

7. CHASSIS
----------
Files: Chasis.SLDPRT, Chasis_final.SLDPRT
Role: Structural base mounting all components.
History: V1 (curved, dropped early) -> V2 (straight array,
         diagonal slots for tolerance) -> V2 Final (slots removed
         for fixed holes, width reduced to fit print bed flat).
Status: V2 Final is current. No adjustable mounts remain.
Open items: Print material, wall thickness, final dimensions.

8. BATTERY
----------
Part: 2 x 2.7V Li-ion batteries
Note: Verify actual cell datasheet - 2.7V nominal is unusually
      low for standard Li-ion, double check chemistry/rating.
Open items: Series or parallel config, capacity (mAh), protection
            circuit.

9. BATTERY HOLDER
------------------
Part: TBD
Role: Holds the 2 Li-ion cells, seats into chassis recess.
Open items: Exact part, terminal type.

10. BUCK CONVERTER
-------------------
Part: TBD
Role: Steps battery voltage down to ESP32 supply voltage.
Open items: Input/output voltage once battery config confirmed.

11. FASTENERS
--------------
Part: M2.0 nuts and screws
Role: Secures all mounted parts to chassis.
Note: Fixed holes in V2 Final need correct tolerance for M2.0
      screws to seat properly in printed holes.

12. BRACKET
------------
Part: Bracket.SLDPRT (render: Bracket-1.PNG)
Role: Supporting structural part in the assembly.
Open items: Exact function/mounting location to be documented.

